sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor V as Visitor
    participant JS as chat.js
    participant RL as RateLimiter ("chat")
    participant CH as ChatModel (/Chat)
    participant KA as KeywordChatAssistant
    participant SK as ShopKnowledge
    participant CA as ICatalog

    Note over V,CA: The support chat "Pip". Not an AI service: a keyword lookup inside the app.<br/>Nothing leaves the server, nothing is stored, nothing costs money.

    V->>JS: types a question, or clicks an example
    JS->>CH: POST /Chat (message, lang, previous question, antiforgery token)
    CH->>RL: 20 questions per minute per IP?
    alt over the limit
        RL-->>JS: 429
        JS-->>V: "wait a minute and try again"
    else within the limit
        CH->>CH: antiforgery token valid?<br/>question 1-200 characters?
        alt too long or empty
            CH-->>JS: "write a question of at most 200 characters"
        else ok
            CH->>KA: Reply(question, english, previous)

            alt contains an email address or 8+ digits in a row
                KA-->>CH: "please don't type personal details here"
                Note over KA: Checked first, before anything is looked up.
            else about how the site is built or protected
                KA-->>CH: "that's not something I answer"
            else about orders, accounts, customers or staff
                KA-->>CH: "I can't see orders or accounts"
            else sounds like a sick animal
                KA-->>CH: "contact a vet" - never a diagnosis
            else something it can work out
                KA->>CA: catalogue, opening hours, ShippingCalculator, food list
                KA-->>CH: open now? / shipping for 3 kg / cage size for 4 /<br/>animals for sale / yes-or-no on a food
            else a lookup
                KA->>SK: Build(catalog)
                SK->>CA: Animals, Accessories (public data only)
                SK-->>KA: one fact per animal, product, food,<br/>FAQ entry, care-guide paragraph, delivery rule
                KA->>KA: fold letters, synonyms, spelling correction,<br/>score by how rare each matching word is,<br/>require more than half the question covered
                alt a fact matches
                    KA-->>CH: answer worded for the question<br/>(advice first, price first, or a short list)
                else nothing matches
                    opt a follow-up ("what does she cost?")
                        KA->>KA: try again with the subject<br/>of the previous question added
                    end
                    KA-->>CH: "I don't know that" + up to 3 questions it can answer
                end
            end

            CH-->>JS: JSON { answer, suggestions }
            JS->>JS: textContent, never innerHTML
            JS-->>V: answer, and suggestion buttons if any
        end
    end

    Note over KA,SK: The real boundary is what ShopKnowledge contains: no orders, accounts,<br/>customers or staff, and nothing about logins, the database or security.<br/>A refused previous question is thrown away, never used as context.
